# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.aot. BuildKit prefers a
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the context-root `.dockerignore`, so
# the AOT image gets its own list without disturbing the JIT one.
#
# The AOT image compiles from source inside the build stage, so it needs
# the opposite of what the JIT image needs: the sources and the MSBuild
# scaffolding in, and the host-side ./artifacts/ publish output out.
**/bin/
**/obj/
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
artifacts/
tests/
docs/
plans/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings
TestResults/
coverage/
.dotnet/
.husky/

# Markdown is excluded wholesale by the JIT context; here two files are
# build inputs — IviCli.Cli.csproj packs README.md and copies
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md into the publish layout so the bundled
# assemblies' attribution travels with the binary.
*.md
!README.md
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
